<title>USA: Alcoa unit reaches tentative pact with UAW.</title>
<headline>Alcoa unit reaches tentative pact with UAW.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aluminum Co of America said on Thursday its Alcoa Forged Products unit in Cleveland and the United Automobile Workers (UAW) reached a tentative labor agreement.</p>
<p>The union has been on strike since September 4 when talks failed to result in a new labor agreement, Alcoa said.</p>
<p>The tentative agreement covering 1,100 workers was reached early this morning after an extended bargaining session mediated by the Federal Mediation and Conciliation Service, Alcoa said.  The agreement is scheduled for a ratification vote by members of UAW Local 1050 on Friday, September 27.</p>
</text>
